       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 4,250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release, 850 mg three times daily) in adults. Many guidelines use 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 4,250 mg in one dose is about 5 times the largest usual single dose of 850 mg. It would risk severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** (not a standard tablet strength, so probably not this one)\n- **500 mg** by mouth twice or three times daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth twice daily with meals\n\nTell me the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or pharmacist if you're unsure. If you really do intend 4,250 mg per dose, please review it with your attending before I enter it."
